  "step": 0.02,
  "airframe": "Fighter1, Multirole1, SmallFighter1, trainer, VTOLTrainer1, CAS1, COIN, EW1, FastBomber1, Darkreach",
  "note": "REPLACES alpha-sweep as the AoA-ceiling instrument. alpha-sweep failed structurally: its demand comes from deriveAzRate (a fraction of the airframe's own STRUCTURAL G), which is an AZIMUTH sweep, so the roll/turn channel saturated first and all 60 R39 segments railed on bank clamp (74-97%), turn-rate cap (85-97%) and blend rail (81-96%) while aoaAboveCeilingPct read 0.0 on 60 of 60. The deficit was paid in ALTITUDE (525-2428 m of descent, q RISING 3-32%), so more demand bought LESS AoA on 7 of 8 lanes. THE FIX IS THE PLANE OF THE PULL, NOT THE SIZE OF IT. This card pulls in the VERTICAL plane: az is identically 0 for every sample of every segment, so the load is carried by pitch alone. THREE of the four rails scorecard.py can report are then unreachable BY CONSTRUCTION, and the fourth is NOT -- corrected 2026-08-02 against the flown R40 batch. bankClampActivePct, turnRateCapActivePct and turnRateDemandRatio all derive from the commanded bank (bankClampActivePct reads bankTR; the other two recover des = |tan(bankTR)|*g/v), and a zero-azimuth demand drives none of them: measured exactly 0.0000 on all 144 segments, with max|targetBank| and max|bankTR| literally 0.000 on all 18,436 scored rows. A NON-ZERO READING ON ANY OF THOSE THREE IS A LAW BUG REPORT -- it would mean the roll channel generated bank against a demand that never asked for any. blendRailPct IS NOT ONE OF THEM AND MUST NOT BE READ AS ONE: bWt = MAX(bigTurn, lateralHold) (ChaseController.cs:2062) and a 72-degree vertical pull MAXIMISES bigTurn, so blendRailPct reads 34-66% on the fast arm, which is expected and correct, not a defect. lateralHold never exceeds 0.10 on this card and never wins the max. It is also the only stimulus that can exceed n = 3.24 under this law at all: a level turn is capped at 1/cos(72 deg) by the bank clamp, and the fighters need n = 4.5-6.4 to reach their own alpha ceiling at corner speed. And the aircraft CLIMBS, so q falls -- the opposite sign to alpha-sweep's dive. TWO RATES, DELIBERATELY, because one cannot serve the roster: corner speed does NOT normalise stall margin (V_corner/V_stall spans 1.50 on Darkreach to 3.90 on EW1), so the 1-g AoA fraction at this entry already spans ~0.65 to ~0.11 before any demand is applied. alphaHoldFast (18 deg/s, 4 s, 72 deg) is the HIGH-LOAD arm and runs FIRST, off the pristine placement, because its load is n = cos(theta) + V*omega/g and it is the entry-speed-sensitive one; it is what exposes Multirole1 and Fighter1, and it is the fast AoA transient the v0.61 4-deg fade floor exists to keep graded. alphaHoldSlow (4 deg/s, 12 s, 48 deg) is the SLOW-APPROACH arm and runs second, because it derives most of its AoA from the deceleration WITHIN the segment and so is robust to a degraded start; it walks the lim-10 group (trainer, EW1, Darkreach) straight across the 0.529-vs-0.7059 onset band that separates the shipped absolute-degree clamps from the unclamped proportional form. The 18 s arm between them is the recovery from a 72 deg zoom -- read spd at the first sample of alphaHoldSlow before reading anything else on that segment. NO MIRROR PUSH, a deliberate exception to the mirrored-pair rule (cards/README.md lists three others): alpha-steps is unchanged and remains the mirrored transient card and the R35 comparison baseline, and adding a push here would double a card whose question is the POSITIVE ceiling. gateMinDn is therefore expected at 1.000 and is non-exposure, not a pass. ENTRY: 1.15x the lane airframe's own FBW corner speed. Not 1.0x -- Darkreach's corner is 100 m/s and its density-corrected stall at 8000 m is ~102 m/s, so 1.0x is below stall for that lane. Not 1.2x either -- CAS1 (0.95*Vmax = 195.3) and COIN (134.6) clear it by under 2%, and 1.15x restores ~6% of margin. All TEN fixed-wing keys clear the v0.92 envelope gate here, against eight for the absolute 250 m/s the alpha-* pair used to fly. THROTTLE IS PINNED AT 0.40, AND THAT IS PART OF THE MEASUREMENT, NOT HOUSEKEEPING. A card that declares an entry speed only SETS it once, at the placement; nothing holds it. R37 measured oblique-6-dwell drifting 1.10x (CAS1) to 2.04x (Darkreach) across ONE capture at the 0.70 default, and the STOL batch is the extreme case -- stol-* declared 90 m/s and reached 340-381 m/s by their last scored segment. Here the risk is ONE-SIDED: drift UP raises q, raises n_max_aero and LOWERS AoA/ceiling, which is exactly the exposure this card needs; drift DOWN reinforces the sweep the card is built on. So the throttle is biased low rather than set to hold. 0.40 is an already-flown operating point (oblique-6-dwell-t040) and is above the MinThrottle 0.25 floor below which EntryThrottle silently snaps back to the 0.70 default. The lane at risk is Multirole1, the lowest predicted exposure (0.81 on alphaHoldFast): CHECK ITS spd AT THE FIRST SAMPLE OF alphaHoldFast before reading its gate. This card does NOT use deriveAzRate, so the RateMaxDegS=30 clip that invalidates stol-sweep's equal-fraction-of-g premise on 4 of 10 lanes does not touch it. ALTITUDE STAYS AT 8000 m: lowering it raises q, which is the wrong direction and was checked and rejected. Darkreach is PAST its ceiling from the first sample by design -- it is the lane that finally exposes aoaRecoverActivePct, which is identically zero below the ceiling and has never fired in the corpus. Full derivation, per-lane predictions and the fire/fail/not-exposed reading of every criterion: cards/ALPHA-CARD-REDESIGN.md. C5 IS AN ALARM, NOT A PASS CRITERION (corrected 2026-08-02). aoaRecoverActivePct is identically zero below the ceiling by construction (ChaseController.cs:1280) and the AoA guard exists precisely to prevent the crossing, so C5 can only ever fire on a segment where C1 or C2 have ALREADY failed. Read it as an alarm: aoaAboveCeilingPct > 0 with aoaRecoverActivePct = 0 is the real defect (the wing crossed the ceiling and nothing flew the recovery); aoaRecoverActivePct > 0 says the recovery bias exists but the guard let the crossing happen; both zero is the healthy case and is NOT EXPOSED for the recovery term, never a pass for it. FLOWN 2026-08-02 AS THE R40 BASELINE AND VALIDATED -- C1 passes 9 of 9 on the fast arm, replicate sigma on gateMinUp <= 0.011, every lane entered from 8000 +/-33 m. DO NOT RE-FLY IT AS A BASELINE: the baseline exists. Its next flight is the SECOND arm of an A/B against the #66 aoaFade law fix, which has not been written yet.",
